#> tool: awkrepl
#> wait: the red door
#> pause: 40
#> must: the red door and the red ring
#> must: a puce coat stays puce
#> not: scarlet door
#> source: gsub
# 13. Find and replace, on selected lines only. Pement:
#   awk '{gsub(/scarlet|ruby|puce/, "red"); print}'       every line
#   awk '/baz/{gsub(/foo/, "bar")};{print}'                only lines with baz
# gsub replaces all matches in $0 (sub replaces the first). Here only lines
# that mention "door" are recoloured; the coat keeps its colour.
# Try: drop the /door/ pattern and watch the coat turn red too.
/door/ { gsub(/scarlet|ruby|puce/, "red") }; { print }

#DATA
the scarlet door and the ruby ring
a puce coat stays puce
one more ruby door
